# deploy/scripts/host.env.example — per-host overrides for lib.sh.
#
# Copy to host.env in this same directory. host.env is git-excluded
# (.gitignore rule: deploy/scripts/**/*.env); this example IS tracked.
#
# host.env is DATA, not code — lib.sh parses it, never sources it, so nothing
# in it can execute. The format is strict:
#
#   - one KEY=VALUE per line; the value is everything after the first `=`,
#     taken literally (no quoting, no expansion). Whitespace around the line
#     and a Windows line ending are tolerated and stripped.
#   - allowed keys: DEPLOYMENT, CONFIG, GPU_IDS — each at most once;
#     DEPLOYMENT must be one token of letters, digits, - and _ (the name
#     becomes ~/.archi/archi-<name>, which the deploy's --force path removes,
#     so a path separator in the name is refused)
#     (a duplicate key aborts: first-wins would let a stale line silently
#     shadow an appended correction)
#   - DEPLOYMENT and CONFIG need a non-empty value (an empty identity would
#     fall through to the reserved default and silently retarget); GPU_IDS=
#     with an empty value is the documented explicit disable
#   - comments (#, indented ok), whitespace-only and blank lines are fine
#   - ANY other line aborts EVERY script that reads lib.sh — status.sh and
#     nuke.sh included: with an unparsable host.env the deployment identity
#     is ambiguous, and failing closed beats tearing down the wrong
#     deployment. The error names the offending line; fix this file.
#
# Precedence: command-line environment > host.env > tracked default. A value
# here applies only when the variable is not already set, so a one-off on the
# command line always wins:
#     DEPLOYMENT=elsewhere ./redeploy.sh
# For DEPLOYMENT/CONFIG an EMPTY environment value counts as unset — an empty
# identity is never valid, so it cannot bypass this file's pin. For GPU_IDS,
# empty stays the explicit disable. Contract pinned by test_host_env.sh.
#
# The config pin (CONFIG_REF / CONFIG_SHA / CONFIG_REPO) is deliberately NOT
# accepted here: it stays overridable per-invocation only, never from a
# persistent git-excluded file.
#
# Reserved names (issue #363):
#   dev   — the GPU host (holygpu7c0717 / archi.rc.fas.harvard.edu), the only
#           production deployment. It needs no host.env: with no file, lib.sh
#           resolves exactly the tracked defaults.
#   claw  — the no-GPU / no-local-vLLM developer workstation.

# --- GPU host (holygpu7c0717) — no host.env needed; shown for completeness ---
# DEPLOYMENT=dev
# GPU_IDS stays at the tracked default (empty): both containers are configured
# `device: cpu`, and on this host the GPUs are owned by the vLLM servers.

# --- no-GPU workstation -------------------------------------------------------
# DEPLOYMENT=claw
# CONFIG=deploy/fasrc-dev/config.yaml
